    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0356" n="282" xml:id="pg282"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 389.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 12, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your dispatch No. 244, of the 19th ultimo,
                    on the subject of the indemnity from Japan under the convention of Yokohama, has
                    been received.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to state that the proposal contained in the verbal note which
                    accompanied that communication is concurred in by the Executive, subject to the
                    constitutional approval of the Senate of the United States. You may, however,
                    regard the proposal as definitively accepted by us.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow</hi>, Esq.,<hi rendition="#italic">
                            &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
